<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="108" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Bicep: recreate sprk-provisioning-jobs queue with sessions + dedup (C5.4/C4.6) + drain-verify runbook</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-1 -- Foundation</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Live queue delete+recreate is a destructive Azure operation with an irreversible in-flight-message-loss window; touches Bicep AND live Azure state per the parent task's Wave G-1 description. FULL + prescriptive steps.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified IaC diff (Bicep resource block) plus a scripted, documented live-surgery sequence -- not itself an architectural decision (already locked), Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, dispatcher, azure-deployment, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Declare the sprk-provisioning-jobs queue in platform-controlplane.bicep (it currently appears in NO Bicep file -- grep-verified 0 hits in infrastructure/; the fleet namespace is out-of-stamp and modules/service-bus.bicep applies uniform properties to ITS OWN queue list, wrong shape for this queue) as a child resource of an `existing` reference to the fleet Service Bus namespace, with requiresDuplicateDetection:true, duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow:'PT1H', requiresSession:true (per the owner-locked session-serialized dispatch decision, DS-2/DS-2b), lockDuration:'PT5M', maxDeliveryCount:10, deadLetteringOnMessageExpiration:true. Both requiresDuplicateDetection and requiresSession are CREATE-TIME-ONLY properties in Azure Service Bus -- the existing live queue (created via bare az servicebus queue create defaults: dedup OFF, sessions OFF) CANNOT be patched. Execute the documented delete-and-recreate live sequence as a runbook (not automated tooling): discard the 1 stale H0 envelope belonging to the C4.5-deleted dead test run, az servicebus queue delete, deploy the Bicep-declared queue, verify properties + that namespace-scope RBAC survived deletion (no re-grant needed).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer / Azure infrastructure operator. Expert in Azure Service Bus queue create-time-only properties, Bicep `existing` cross-scope resource references, and safe destructive-operation runbooks.</role>

  <goal>platform-controlplane.bicep declares the sprk-provisioning-jobs queue as a Bicep-managed resource with sessions ON, dedup ON (PT1H window), matching the DS-2-locked session-serialized dispatch decision. A documented runbook (this task's notes + a checked-in script if warranted) executes the live delete-recreate on the dev stamp: az servicebus queue show confirms the property values post-recreate.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-5 §C4.6 (grep-verified) confirms: infrastructure/bicep/modules/service-bus.bicep:39 sets requiresDuplicateDetection:false uniformly for its managed queues (default queueNames ['sdap-jobs','document-indexing'] at :15) and sprk-provisioning-jobs is in NEITHER that list NOR any other Bicep file. The live queue was created via bare az CLI defaults. ServiceBusHandlerEnqueuer.cs's header (lines 11-45) documents it ALREADY sets SessionId=CustomerId on every message specifically so 'a future toggle to requiresSession=true works without code change' -- this task is that toggle. DS-2 §2.3 point 5 calls this queue recreation a HARD PREREQUISITE for task 102's session processor (a session receiver against a non-session queue fails loudly at StartProcessingAsync, which is the correct NFR-05 posture, but only once this task lands).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/service-bus.bicep</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/membership-topic.bicep</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Enqueue/ServiceBusHandlerEnqueuer.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-22">L2 handler execution is session-serialized per customer: ServiceBusSessionProcessor with SessionId=CustomerId, MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession=1 is a HARD-CODED correctness invariant (not a tunable) protecting the 39 ETag-guarded ReplaceRunAsync call sites from cross-handler races (DS-2b Sec.0-1). Retry authority is Sec.4C RollbackTransitions, never an SB Abandon-loop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-5 §C4.6">requiresDuplicateDetection and requiresSession are CREATE-TIME-ONLY Azure Service Bus queue properties -- the live queue MUST be deleted and recreated, not patched. duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow MUST be &gt;= the longest reconciler retry re-enqueue window for the same paramHash -- PT1H is the documented safe floor (handlers run &lt;=30-60 min per DS-2b §1.2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-5 §C4.6">Blast radius: destructive to in-flight messages -- SAFE TODAY (exactly 1 stale H0 envelope belonging to the C4.5-deleted dead test run exists). This is a one-time safe window; document the runbook so a FUTURE queue-property change (post-go-live) is a coordinated drain, not an ad-hoc delete.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Three-question component-justification gate applies to any NEW class/interface/Bicep resource/script this task introduces. Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing are pre-answered in &lt;notes&gt; below; cite them verbatim in the PR description per root CLAUDE.md §11 enforcement table.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Provisioning queue recreation with sessions + dedup</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds5-cat456-remediation.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds2-dispatcher-design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read DS-5 §C5.4/§C4.6 in full plus membership-topic.bicep as the RBAC-pattern reference (task 110 reuses it).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Bicep resource">In platform-controlplane.bicep, add `resource sbNamespace 'Microsoft.ServiceBus/namespaces@...' existing = { name: serviceBusNamespaceName }` (new param) plus a child `queues` resource 'sprk-provisioning-jobs' with the exact property block from this task's prompt.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Validate">az bicep build -- zero new errors.</step>
    <step order="3" name="What-if">az deployment sub what-if confirms the queue as Create (or, if a same-named queue already exists live, confirms Bicep would attempt an in-place property change that Azure will REJECT for create-time-only properties -- this confirms the delete-first requirement empirically before touching live state).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Pre-check">az servicebus queue message-count (or portal) confirms exactly the 1 expected stale message; discard/purge it.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Delete">az servicebus queue delete --name sprk-provisioning-jobs (dev namespace).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Deploy">az deployment sub create with the Bicep template -- creates the queue with the new properties.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Verify">az servicebus queue show --query 'requiresDuplicateDetection,requiresSession,duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow' -- confirms true/true/PT1H.</step>
    <step order="8" name="RBAC survival check">Confirm namespace-scope RBAC (to be granted in task 110) is unaffected by the queue-level delete/recreate (namespace-scope grants are not queue-scoped).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If az servicebus queue message-count shows MORE than the 1 expected stale message at step 4 (indicating live traffic this task's authors did not anticipate), STOP before deleting -- escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than discarding unknown in-flight work. This is destructive and irreversible.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az servicebus">queue show/delete/message-count</tool>
    <tool name="az bicep">build/what-if</tool>
    <tool name="az deployment">sub create</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="infra">infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep (modified)</output>
    <output type="runbook">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/queue-recreate-runbook-2026-08.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">az bicep build infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'requiresSession' infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep shows true; grep 'requiresDuplicateDetection' shows true; grep 'duplicateDetectionHistoryTimeWindow' shows PT1H.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-recreate: az servicebus queue show --name sprk-provisioning-jobs --query requiresSession returns true (live verification on dev).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-recreate: az servicebus queue show --name sprk-provisioning-jobs --query requiresDuplicateDetection returns true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The runbook note documents the exact delete/recreate command sequence + the pre-check message count observed, for repeatability on prod/other stamps.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the queue exists live today with wrong (default) properties; service-bus.bicep's uniform-queue-properties shape does not fit this queue (different dedup/session requirements than sdap-jobs/document-indexing). Extension -- cannot extend service-bus.bicep's shared queue list without forcing this queue's properties onto unrelated queues, or vice versa; a dedicated resource block in platform-controlplane.bicep (the L2 stamp's own file) is correct. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- task 102's session processor throws immediately at StartProcessingAsync against a non-session queue; L1 SB dedup stays permanently inert, leaving task 107's attempt-field fix with nothing to protect against.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
